"""HOOLA PROMPTING P0 NAAP - the asks (docs/HOOLA_PROMPTING_PLAN.md part 11, P0).

60 rough asks of the kind a real owner types, 20 per section (web / image / script), half Hinglish and half English.
Every ask carries TWO forms of the same job:

- `raw`   = her rough line, exactly as she would type it.
- `brief` = the same job with the missing details filled in BY HAND, in the section's anatomy (the parts a complete
            ask has). This is what a perfect HOOLA PROMPTING would hand the engine after reading her context and
            asking its questions - so the card measures the CEILING of the idea, not a compiler that does not exist.

`must`  = what she actually wanted, as things a program (web / script) or a picture reader (image) can check.
`facts` = short literal strings from the brief (a price, a date, a time) that must appear unchanged in the result;
          a fact given as a list = any one of those spellings (a Hinglish script may say '5 baje' for '5 am').

Nothing here is a real business; names, prices and numbers are made up for the card. Phone numbers are never used.
"""
